@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-VIZ-001 THE ELEMENT CONTOURS (ADR-046). The exact invocation,
rem recorded so the run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, TWENTY-SIX in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem                        sha1sum         244b38de8feac0475af7cdc56ba9415d27d8dd29
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem                        sha1sum         afd0197d4f4726db7f533c2f27f4f6e069ba83c6
rem
rem BOTH FORMS ARE RECORDED because they differ and a hash without its
rem algorithm cannot be checked: .gitattributes sets `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, so
rem git stores LF while the working tree is CRLF.
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: 16 logical cores let `cmake --build` run 18 compiles at once, and
rem a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units exhausted the
rem commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens nothing -- same sources, same
rem flags, -Werror included. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT CHANGED SINCE 974b62b, AND WHAT IS OWED BY IT.
rem
rem   MODIFIED     include/bettercad/renderer/MeshView.hpp
rem                src/renderer/MeshView.cpp
rem                               A QUALIFIED P16 FILE. One new MeshSource
rem                               enumerator, VolumeBoundaryByTetrahedron, and
rem                               one new factory,
rem                               volumeBoundaryByTetrahedronOf, with the
rem                               face-incidence helper it needs.
rem                tests/renderer/MeshViewTests.cpp
rem                               13 -> 20 cases.
rem                tests/renderer/StructuralResultViewTests.cpp
rem                               66 -> 69 cases.
rem
rem   NOT CHANGED  THE MESHING MODULE, AT ALL. Zero diff in src/meshing and
rem                include/bettercad/meshing, verified against HEAD -- which
rem                is the whole point of this increment and is stated as a
rem                measured fact rather than an intention.
rem                StructuralContour, also at all. triangleCornerBands reads
rem                elementOfTriangle and looks the id up in the field, so a
rem                view whose element ids are tetrahedra simply works.
rem
rem THE BLOCKER THIS INCREMENT REMOVES WAS A WRONG CONCLUSION FROM A CORRECT
rem DIAGNOSIS, and it stood for two milestones in TODO.md, REMAINING_SCOPE.md
rem and ADR-044's own title. It said a boundary-view element contour needed a
rem new capability in the qualified P16 meshing module -- a
rem triangle-to-owning-tetrahedron mapping -- and that this was a scope
rem decision.
rem
rem Every fact was right. volumeBoundaryOf names Triangle3 elements, an element
rem channel is per TETRAHEDRON, and meshing::Triangle carries no owning
rem tetrahedron. But the question "which tetrahedron owns this triangle" ONLY
rem ARISES IF THE BOUNDARY IS TAKEN FROM THE TRIANGLE3 ELEMENTS. Deriving it
rem from the tetrahedra gives ownership by construction, because the
rem tetrahedron is in hand when the face is emitted. ADR-046 records the two
rem routes that were rejected, and ADR-044 now carries a partial-supersede
rem notice rather than being quietly left wrong.
rem
rem THE MEASUREMENT THIS RUN PROTECTS, and it is an INDEPENDENT one: the
rem tet-derived boundary covers EXACTLY the same node triples as the Triangle3
rem boundary. The two are built from different data by different code, so
rem comparing them checks each against something other than what produced it.
rem Asserted BOTH directions, with the counts required equal first and each
rem set's size required to equal the triangle count, so it cannot pass on a
rem subset or hide a duplicated face.
rem
rem And the winding is checked AGAINST THE SOLID, not against kTetFaces: the
rem block fixture is convex, so every outward normal has a positive component
rem along (face centroid - body centre). A test that re-used the face table
rem would have proved only that the table was applied consistently -- and
rem probe E3, which emits the sorted key instead of the wound face, produces
rem the right faces in the right places with arbitrary normals. Only the
rem analytic check sees it.
rem
rem All seven element channels contour the boundary: von Mises, StressXX,
rem StressYY, StressZZ, StressXY, StressYZ, StressZX. On screen the contour
rem shows 7 distinct colours against a uniform fill's 1.
rem
rem MUTATION: 8 probe runs over 7 distinct mutations, ALL SEVEN KILLED.
rem E7 -- the non-manifold refusal -- survived the first batch, and I was
rem about to record it as an unreachable guard. That was wrong: MeshBuilder is
rem public and addTetrahedron checks CONNECTIVITY ONLY, because whether four
rem points enclose a positive volume is a whole-mesh question its header says
rem validation answers later. So a non-manifold mesh can be built by hand, the
rem guard is reachable, and E7 was a REAL GAP. It is now killed by a case that
rem builds three tetrahedra sharing one face, paired with a two-tetrahedron
rem discriminator -- because without one the refusal would also be satisfied
rem by a factory that rejected ANY shared face, which would reject every real
rem volume mesh.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. THE FILTER IS UNCHANGED: `unit\.Mesh`
rem already covers unit.MeshView as a substring and `unit\.Structural` covers
rem unit.StructuralViz, so this increment's ten new cases are selected without
rem a new term. The SELECTED COUNT IS RECORDED BY THIS RUN rather than
rem predicted here -- a figure nobody has measured does not belong in the
rem evidence for a run.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem thirteen milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so
rem repeating one measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's.
rem They still run UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
